# The image corpus is a deterministic function of the code and the seed in
# configs/dataset_v1.yaml. Committing ~0.9 GiB of derived JPEGs would make the
# repository permanently expensive to clone and would add nothing the seed does
# not already determine. Everything needed to REGENERATE the images is tracked;
# a curated sample is committed under docs/samples/ so a reviewer can see the
# corpus without building it.
dataset/data/**/images/
dataset/data/**/_crops/

# 21 MB per rebuild, and fully regenerated. manifest.csv (2.3 MB) IS tracked and
# carries the same index in a form you can open in a spreadsheet.
dataset/data/**/manifest.jsonl

# build noise
dataset/logs/
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
venv/
*.egg-info/
.DS_Store

# LaTeX build products
paper/*.aux
paper/*.log
paper/*.out
paper/*.toc
paper/*.pdf
!paper/figures/*.pdf

# Experiment artefacts that are derived and too large for git.
# Resize cache (~1.4 GB of PNGs) is rebuilt by experiments/build_resize_cache.py;
# its per-image SHA-256 list and aggregate hash ARE tracked in
# experiments/cache_fingerprints/ so a rebuilt cache can be verified.
experiments/cache/
# 224 MB pHash pair list; exceeds GitHub's 100 MB per-file limit.
# Regenerate with experiments/verify_near_duplicates.py; summary is in NEAR_DUPLICATE_AUDIT.md.
experiments/near_duplicate_candidates.csv
# Local smoke-test builds of the generator (6 persons), not the frozen corpus.
dataset/data/sample/
# Local virtual environments
.venv-*/

# E2 checkpoints (~95 MB each); configs, logs and scores ARE tracked.
experiments/e2_visual/runs/**/*.pt
